---
import CodeBlock from '../../components/code-block.astro';
import GuidePage from '../../layouts/guide-page.astro';
---

<GuidePage
  title="CLI"
  lead="Three commands: set a project up, proof its theme, and check it keeps the laws. No telemetry."
>
  <h2 id="init">nib init</h2>
  <p>
    Asks for a preset and how CSS is loaded (or takes <code>--preset</code>, <code>--css plain|tailwind</code> and
    <code>--dir</code>), then writes <code>nib.config.json</code>, a CSS entry and an empty theme file. Files already
    there are kept, and an existing config's choices win.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock label="shell" code={`npx @nib-ui/cli init --preset dashboard --css tailwind`} />

  <h2 id="theme-check">nib theme check</h2>
  <p>
    Reads the <code>--nib-*</code> colours of your theme file (or the files given), lays them over Nib's palette and
    proofs both themes. Errors exit with 1, so it fits in CI.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    label="output"
    code={`Pulling a proof of src/nib-theme.css…
error    Proof mark: accent on paper-raised is 2.8:1, needs 3:1.
Not locked up: 1 error, 4 warnings.`}
  />

  <h2 id="lint">nib lint</h2>
  <p>
    Runs Nib's own Stylelint rules over your CSS and scans class names in HTML, JSX, Vue, Svelte and Astro for Tailwind
    utilities that bring back radius, shadows, gradients, blur or colours outside the tokens. A
    <code>nib-lint-ignore</code> comment waives its line and the next.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    label="output"
    code={`Setting type: 42 files…
src/card.vue:2:19  nib/no-shadow  shadow-lg: nothing casts a shadow.
Not locked up: 1 proof mark in 1 file.`}
  />
</GuidePage>
